Let $C_{T|F}$ be the personal cost of trying and then failing. Let $C_N$ be the personal cost of not trying. Let $D_J$ be the burden of ending up in a job, and let $R_N$ be the regret attached to never making the attempt. The speaker’s comparison can be reconstructed as: $\begin{aligned}
C_{T|F} &\approx D_J, \\
C_N &\approx D_J + R_N.\end{aligned}$ Subtracting the first line from the second gives: $\begin{aligned}
C_N - C_{T|F}
&\approx (D_J + R_N) - D_J \\
&= R_N.\end{aligned}$ So, within this simplified comparison, $R_N > 0
\qquad \Longrightarrow \qquad
C_N > C_{T|F}.$

