p.src:
The durable principle is therefore careful rather than reckless: $\text{recoverable downside}
\quad \text{must be compared with} \quad
\text{durable regret of inaction}.$ That is the chapter’s working contribution to the broader entrepreneurship book. Risk is not measured only by what can go wrong. It is also measured by what a person may have to live with if he never tries.

